\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The protocol turns narrow local teachers into a single, broadly capable model. Under heterogeneous data ($\alpha =0.05$, $N=10$), the global model (blue) reaches three to four times the accuracy of the average local teacher and comes within a few points of the centralized reference, on both vision (ViT-B/32, CIFAR-100) and language (RoBERTa, MPNet, AG-News). The frozen backbone never enters the encrypted aggregation, so the protocol and its cost are unchanged across these scales.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scaling}{{3}{9}{The protocol turns narrow local teachers into a single, broadly capable model. Under heterogeneous data ($\alpha =0.05$, $\Nc =10$), the global model (blue) reaches three to four times the accuracy of the average local teacher and comes within a few points of the centralized reference, on both vision (ViT-B/32, CIFAR-100) and language (RoBERTa, MPNet, AG-News). The frozen backbone never enters the encrypted aggregation, so the protocol and its cost are unchanged across these scales}{figure.3}{}}
\newlabel{fig:scaling@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][8][]9}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Neither ingredient suffices alone ($\alpha =0.05$). On CIFAR-100, distillation without a shared basin stays at chance, because updates from different initializations do not combine; the shared basin makes the same linear combination work. On MNIST the no-basin variant recovers partially but still trails the full method. In both cases the full method is best and approaches the centralized reference (dashed).}}{9}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:necessity}{{4}{9}{Neither ingredient suffices alone ($\alpha =0.05$). On CIFAR-100, distillation without a shared basin stays at chance, because updates from different initializations do not combine; the shared basin makes the same linear combination work. On MNIST the no-basin variant recovers partially but still trails the full method. In both cases the full method is best and approaches the centralized reference (dashed)}{figure.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:necessity@cref}{{[figure][4][]4}{[1][8][]9}{}{}{}}
