\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Distillation never hurts and adds most where the basin is weak. Each point is a basin source at a given heterogeneity $\alpha $ (MNIST, $N=10$); the horizontal axis is the accuracy of the shared basin $\theta _0$ on its own and the vertical axis the accuracy of the resulting global model. All points lie above the no-lift diagonal, and the gap is largest when the basin is weakest.}}{11}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:continuum}{{7}{11}{Distillation never hurts and adds most where the basin is weak. Each point is a basin source at a given heterogeneity $\alpha $ (MNIST, $\Nc =10$); the horizontal axis is the accuracy of the shared basin $\thz $ on its own and the vertical axis the accuracy of the resulting global model. All points lie above the no-lift diagonal, and the gap is largest when the basin is weakest}{figure.7}{}}
